# Regex literal duplicate flag rejected

Verifies a repeated `g` flag is rejected at compile time: no regex value is
produced and the diagnostic names the duplicated flag with its source span.

>>> source
const bad: regex = /abc/gg
print(bad)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `/abc/gg` for type `regex`: duplicate `g` flag in regex literal at Span { start: 19, end: 26 }

<<< exit
1
